// THE RUNTIME WALK'S EMPTY ARM SLOT IS UNCONSTRUCTIBLE (L5, 2026-09-30).
// This shape reached the evidence walk with a handler whose arm region had
// a gap: `call_b` put the perform behind a frame fence, a second declarer
// of `b` made the op ambiguous for the singleton tier, and the installed
// pair covered one effect's disjoint op sets with the non-declaring handler
// innermost — so `ev_perform_node` had to skip a node whose slot for `b`
// was empty (it once dispatched on whatever was there, exit 15 for 33). A
// handler is exhaustive over every effect its arms answer now: no arm
// region has a gap, and the declaration refuses before any walk exists.
// The runtime skip stays in the emitted walk as the invariant's twin,
// unreachable by construction.
//
// The frontier expects E_HandlerInexhaustive, exit nonzero, zero WAT bytes.
// Before this landing the leg ran it to 33.
effect Two {
  a(n: Int) -> Int
  b(n: Int) -> Int
}

handler ha {
  a(n) => resume(n + 1),
}

handler hb {
  b(n) => resume(n + 2),
}

// A second declarer of `b`, never installed — its only job was to make the
// op ambiguous so the singleton tier declined and the evidence tier answered.
handler hb_alt {
  b(n) => resume(n + 3),
}

fn call_b(n) = b(n)

fn main() = a(10) + call_b(20) ~> ha ~> hb
